---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import { site } from '../lib/site.mjs';
import { flagship } from '../lib/learning-apps.mjs';
import { VP, VS } from '../lib/seismology.mjs';
---
<Layout title="About Earth Science Lab" description="Earth Science Lab makes free interactive earth science simulations for students aged 10–16 and their teachers, from the makers of Interactive Periodic Table." section="About" crumbs={[['About']]}>
  <div class="wrap prose">
    <div class="page-intro">
      <span class="eyebrow">About</span>
      <h1>About Earth Science Lab</h1>
      <p class="lede">{site.tagline} Earth Science Lab is a collection of free, interactive simulations that let students aged about 10 to 16 work like earth scientists.</p>
    </div>
    <h2>What we make</h2>
    <p>Each lab is a small working model you can change, paired with a short explanation, a printable classroom activity and a teacher answer key. There are six labs: the <a href="/tools/earthquake-epicenter/">Earthquake Epicenter Finder</a>, the <a href="/tools/plate-tectonics/">Plate Tectonics Explorer</a>, the <a href="/tools/contour-map/">Contour Map Playground</a>, the <a href="/tools/river-erosion/">River Erosion Sandbox</a>, the <a href="/tools/water-cycle/">Water Cycle Explorer</a> and the <a href="/tools/rock-cycle/">Rock Cycle Builder</a>. <a href="/tools/">See them all</a>.</p>
    <h2>How the models work</h2>
    <p>The labs use real methods with simplified, clearly explained models. In the Epicenter Finder, for example, P waves travel at {VP.toFixed(1)} km/s and S waves at {VS.toFixed(1)} km/s through a uniform crust, which gives the familiar “8.4 kilometers per second of S–P lag” rule. Real rocks are not uniform, and each lab says what its model leaves out.</p>
    <p>The seismograms, the map and its towns are synthetic: they are generated by the model, not taken from real recordings or real places. Worksheets and answer keys are calculated by the same code that runs each lab, and automated tests check that the printed numbers match.</p>
    <h2>Who makes it</h2>
    <p>Earth Science Lab comes from the makers of <a href={flagship.url + '/'}>{flagship.name}</a>, and sits alongside free learning apps for physics, biology, astronomy, geometry and coding linked at the bottom of every page.</p>
    <h2>Accessibility</h2>
    <p>The labs work with a keyboard, respect your device’s reduced-motion setting, and offer typed inputs wherever there is something to drag. If something does not work for you or your students, please tell us.</p>
    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>Questions, corrections and classroom stories are welcome at <a href={`mailto:${site.contactEmail}`}>{site.contactEmail}</a>.</p>
  </div>
</Layout>
